cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use HydroModPy in your work, please cite it using the following metadata."
title: "HydroModPy: a Python toolbox for deploying catchment-scale shallow groundwater models"
abstract: "HydroModPy is an open-source Python toolbox that automates the deployment of shallow groundwater models at catchment scale. It integrates geospatial processing, MODFLOW 6, MODFLOW-NWT, Boussinesq, and GR4J solvers, calibration, validation, and result visualization on Pydantic v2 configurations."
type: software
license: EPL-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/HydroModPy/HydroModPy"
url: "https://docs.hydromodpy.fr/"
# Concept DOI on Zenodo: every version, resolves to the latest archive.
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22141925"
# One DOI per version archived on Zenodo. The Cite page uses the one of the
# version it documents, the concept DOI above for a version not archived.
identifiers:
